# Everything that is not the course itself.
#
# What ships: the notebooks, the module READMEs, the images they embed, and the
# three files that make `uv sync` reproduce the environment. Nothing else.

# Environment. `.python-version` ships: uv.lock pins the packages but not the
# interpreter, and without it a clone builds on whatever Python is newest.
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.Python

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets. Nothing here needs a credential, so anything matching is an accident.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Authoring tools: notebook builders, diagram sources, audits, tests.
# These generate what ships; a reader never runs them.
scripts/
tests/
Makefile
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Diagram sources. Only the PNG and GIF that the notebooks and READMEs
# actually embed are tracked.
assets/fonts/
assets/diagrams/*.svg

# Generated by running the notebooks: scratch training scripts, downloaded
# datasets, profiler traces, benchmark output, and saved plots.
*.png
!assets/diagrams/*.png
*.gif
!assets/diagrams/*.gif
**/scratch-*/
**/profiles/
**/data/
**/*_results*.json
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.log
